Tia (docs): FYI opening a PR to add compact parser examples + shim guidance for nested-array tool outputs and optional fields. Need quick reviews on wording and SDK parity. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1301
Sam (eng-runtime): Thx. Make sure to mention runtimebehavior: when parsing fails we emit telemetry key `parse_shim_applied` and attempt the compact-envelope coercion. Important for SRE.
Tia (docs): Added a short note about that. Planning to show a broken JSON -> shim -> canonical envelope flow.
Jordan (devex): Can we include 2 variants: streaming-safe parse (token-check) and non-streaming retry with shim? I can draft a JS streaming snippet.
Maria (sdk): Here's a compact JS sample; will port to Python after review.
Maria (sdk): ```js
// sdk example: parse-with-shim
const r = await client.responses.create({ model: 'rw-open-7b', input: prompt });
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(r.output_text);
  // handle parsed.result or parsed.actions
} catch (e) {
  // runtime will apply shim; client.responses.parse_shim(r.output_text)
}
```
Sam (eng-runtime): Perfect. Also call out what the client returns: route-level response includes `parsed: "true|false"` and `parse_shim_applied: "true|false"` so callers know when to fall back.
Chad (product): Add a short customer note: Dedicated customers may see extra latency on the retry path; recommend tuning batch size or enabling prefix caching.
Jordan (devex): I'll add an example prompt that reproduces the nested-array case: `Return actions as [[{"name":"x"}]]` and a tiny unit test to validate shim behavior.
Tia (docs): Good. Also spotted some stale anchors under /tooling/structured-output -> I'll run link-check and add redirects.
Maria (sdk): Python snippet (sync) mirror:```py
# python example
resp = client.responses.create(model='rw-open-7b', input=prompt)
try:
    data = json.loads(resp.output_text)
except Exception:
    data = client.responses.parse_shim(resp.output_text)
```
